+Reading from a file
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Use :func:`~rich.progress.open` to read a file while a progress bar shows how many bytes have been read. The default mode is text, which gives you ``str`` from ``read()``. Pass ``"rb"`` to read binary data, which gives you ``bytes``. The total defaults to the size of the file in bytes, so you don't need to pass one::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with rich.progress.open("data.csv") as csv_file:
+        for line in csv_file:
+            ...
+
+    with rich.progress.open("data.bin", "rb") as binary_file:
+        data = binary_file.read()
+
+When the ``with`` block exits, the reader is closed. A missing file raises ``FileNotFoundError`` before the display starts.
+
+To attach the reader to a :class:`~rich.progress.Progress` instance you manage yourself, call :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.open`. It doesn't start the display, so start the ``Progress`` first::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with rich.progress.Progress() as progress:
+        with progress.open("data.csv", description="Reading CSV...") as csv_file:
+            for line in csv_file:
+                ...
+
+Reading from a file-like object
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+If you already have an open binary file object, use :func:`~rich.progress.wrap_file`. It only accepts binary files, and you must give the total number of bytes. The reader does not close the wrapped file when the ``with`` block exits, so you still need to close it yourself::
+
+    import os
+    import rich.progress
+
+    total = os.path.getsize("data.bin")
+    with open("data.bin", "rb") as source:
+        with rich.progress.wrap_file(source, total) as binary_file:
+            data = binary_file.read()
+
+:meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.wrap_file` also accepts a ``task_id``. If that task already has a total, you can leave out ``total``::
+
+    import os
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with rich.progress.Progress() as progress:
+        task_id = progress.add_task("Reading", total=os.path.getsize("data.bin"))
+        with open("data.bin", "rb") as source:
+            reader = progress.wrap_file(source, task_id=task_id)
+            data = reader.read()
+
